        "title": "Watchmaking - 09 Movement Anatomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A mechanical watch movement is a miniature machine that converts 40–70 hours of stored elastic energy into ~1,400,000 regulated pulses per day (at 28,800 vph), maintaining 20–50 µm tolerances over a 50+ year service life, in a package roughly 30 mm in diameter and 3–5 mm thick. The gear train is a ~14,000:1 ratio reduction from the barrel to the escape wheel."
